<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prokop of Moravia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1354–1405</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prokop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> was a margrave of Moravia of the Luxembourg dynasty, the younger son of John Henry and brother of Jobst. He shared Moravia with Jobst but fought him for years in a ruinous struggle, siding with his cousin King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wenceslaus-iv-of-bohemia">Wenceslaus IV of Bohemia</a> against Jobst and Sigismund. Imprisoned by Sigismund from 1402, he died at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brno">Brno</a> in 1405.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prokop-of-moravia.jpg" alt="Prokop of Moravia" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Petr Maixner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prokop_Lucembursk%C3%BD_zajat_bratrancem_Zikmundem_(%C4%8Cesko-moravsk%C3%A1_kronika,_1868).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
